)%p = i, so unite(i,i) does nothing, so comp remains p\n            # But original code says: components = (k > 1) ? dsu.comp : p - dsu.sz.size()\n            # dsu.sz.size() is p, so p - p = 0. That seems wrong.\n            # Actually, looking more carefully: for k=1, the unite(i, i) calls do nothing (unite returns false)\n            # So comp remains p. But the original code uses p - dsu.sz.size() which is p - p = 0.\n            # This seems like a bug in the original code, but let's follow it exactly.\n            components = p - len(sz)\n        \n        for i in range(components):\n            result = (result * p) % MOD\n    \n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00030596344731748104, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.05150304362177849, -0.0001161031104857102, -0.11285834014415741, -0.07199407368898392, -0.0009358317474834621, -0.0001003691868390888, -1.2755313036905136e-05, -0.017886178568005562, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.486063259420916e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.63363116979599, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -0.19800667464733124, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.005251660011708736, -1.5258672647178173e-05, -0.06211281567811966, -7.510157047363464e-06, -4.95898348162882e-05, -1.0490362910786644e-05, -1.0371154530730564e-05, -0.023246610537171364, -1.7046782886609435e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00012420836719684303, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.2755313036905136e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.3484514653682709, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.03245760500431061, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.08894381672143936, -4.768370